      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To study the mechanism of baicalin on the cytokines of Th1/Th2 in murine model of asthma."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "The murine model of asthma was induced by OVA. Different doses of baicalin were orally administered to the mice respectively. The spleen cells were cultured 3 days for the measurement of IFN-gamma, IL-4, IL-5 and IL-10 by ELISA. After 2 days of culture, the spleen cells were treated with Trizol for extraction of total RNA. The gene expressions of T-bet, GATA-3 and STAT-6 were analyzed by RT-PCR."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The treatment with baicalin obviously decreased the production of IL-4 and IL-5 and the gene expression of GATA-3, STAT-6, but increased the production of IL-10."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Baicalin may modulate the Th1/Th2 balance mainly by altering the gene expressions of GATA-3 and STAT-6 in vivo and increasing the production of IL-10."
        }
      ]},
